#
# The Classic graphics' tileset: the art a hex's terrain selects on the 3D board's Classic columns
# (TilesetScenery, BoardArtwork), in the 2D tilesets' format: base/super/ortho <level> "<terrains>" "<theme>"
# "<image;image...>". Image names are relative to data/models/board/classic. A name without an extension is the
# key of art the 3D board never draws as an image: buildings/... (a structure's model), scenery/... and decal/...
# (the layout or decal the legacy conversion turns a token into), quay/... (the fitted quay wall stands for it),
# route (a road: the 3D road system draws it), bridge (both graphics draw the 3D bridge), design (a container
# yard: its design draws it), water (the water animation draws it, tinted or toned; frozen, its still first
# frame under the ice), space (transparent: the sky shows through) and magma (its animated surface covers it).
# Ground art is drawn for level 0 and turned for a hex's level by tileset/levels.json, as the old per-level
# copies were; fungus ground keeps its own level-0 art, its other levels turn terrain/fungus/base_low.png.

